{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKuF3UALnX46iYBi6u7P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved the change for #161 and wrote the report to `.ard/161/review-eng-review.md`.\n\nThe change follows `plan.md`. Wakes coalesce, they go through the normal tick (so the kill switch and job pool still apply), and a wake that arrives during shutdown starts nothing. The new scheduler tests cover each planned scenario, and the docs are updated.\n\n- **Checks run:** `go vet` on the two changed packages is clean, and `go test ./internal/controller ./internal/servecmd -run Wake` passes.\n- **Checks not run:** I did not run the repository's lint target. I did not measure diff coverage. By reading, the new tests exercise every added code path except the `wake_other.go` stub, which isn't built on Unix.\n- **One low, non-blocking finding:** `TestWakeSignals` in `internal/servecmd/wake_unix_test.go` never checks that the forwarder stops after the context is cancelled, which the plan listed. It only calls `cancel()` at the end. A check like that needs care, because once `signal.Stop` has run, SIGUSR1 can kill the test process."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":22346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":681},"output_tokens":370,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"891d4578-dcb0-4abb-8e2f-66dc03559451","uuid":"71ce7d0a-f35f-45f7-8c0f-cac9fb63f199","timestamp":"2026-11-23T13:00:09.987Z","request_id":"req_011ChKuF3LDoHC3Epu3mfkj3"}
